      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-28T00:39:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did debate about where the best place to put it.\nThe existing legacy code lives in power/common.c, and is quite tightly coupled to the power handling, so I saw there was some precedence here.\nIf you suggestions as to where to put it, I would welcome them.\nIt didnt\u0027t seem right to put it in the shim directory, but there are connections to legacy code (the charger hook), so perhaps the shim directory is the best place for it.",
      "parentUuid": "861bd6b5_45023b3b",
      "revId": "13f0e44463d798a32007d81c87f25583a2ad7a93",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d187ddcc_a59c705c",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/hibernate.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-28T00:48:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The other consideration is that this particular piece of code is essentially a port of the legacy code specific to the new AP power sequence code, not so much\nthat it is actually part of it, but that the old code was entangled with the old power code. The new code can only be included when the new power sequence code is used, so there is some dependency here. In some ways I see subsys/ap_power the new version of power/, so perhaps any code replacing that old directory should live in the new directory.\n\nA more \u0027correct\u0027 solution would be to disentangle the hibernation code entirely from the legacy power/common.c, and then allow this to be included in both the old and new, but that seemed like quite a tricky exercise. Maybe that\u0027s a longer term solution.",
      "parentUuid": "a96064d0_2b653409",
      "revId": "13f0e44463d798a32007d81c87f25583a2ad7a93",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09ac77bd_d2a83a99",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/hibernate.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-28T05:19:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the best option is to put this in the legacy tree and don\u0027t include it in EC-OS builds; also make its build conditional on CONFIG_HIBERNATE + AP_PWRSEQ.\nNot unlike what I ended up doing in https://crrev.com/c/3868882, we don\u0027t really have a place for pure-zephyr application code yet so we can toss it in the legacy directory but only build it for zephyr.",
      "parentUuid": "d187ddcc_a59c705c",
      "revId": "13f0e44463d798a32007d81c87f25583a2ad7a93",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
